B.c55=new A.Nw("Safety first","\ud83e\uddba",D.c0,B.doO)
B.c4V=new A.jW("Wire colours","Black is hot (it carries the power), white is neutral (the way back), bare copper or green is ground (the safety path). Red is a second hot, often used for a switched line.")
B.c51=new A.jW("Screw colours","On an outlet the brass screw takes the hot wire, the silver screw takes the neutral and the green screw takes the ground.")
B.c4P=new A.jW("Wire size","14 gauge wire is for 15 amp circuits (lights and outlets). 12 gauge is for 20 amp circuits (kitchens). A thinner wire than the breaker allows can overheat and start a fire.")
B.c4J=new A.jW("Breakers","A breaker is a safety switch. It trips when a circuit carries too much current, so the wires never get hot enough to burn.")
B.c4X=new A.jW("Wire nuts","Strip about 3/4 inch, twist the bare ends together clockwise, and screw on the nut until no bare copper shows. Give each wire a gentle tug.")
B.c52=new A.jW("Switches","A switch cuts the hot wire only. The neutral goes straight through to the light.")
B.c53=new A.jW("GFCI","A GFCI outlet watches the current going out and coming back. If a little leaks (through water or a person) it cuts the power in a fraction of a second.")
B.c4C=new A.jW("Ceiling fans","A fan shakes and is heavy. It needs a box that says fan rated, fixed to the joist, not a plain light box.")
B.c4E=new A.jW("Heights","Outlets sit about 16 inches from the floor. Switches sit about 48 inches up, where your hand falls.")
B.dgJ=w([B.c4V,B.c51,B.c4P,B.c4J,B.c4X,B.c52,B.c53,B.c4C,B.c4E],x.Z)
B.c58=new A.Nw("Wiring basics","\u26a1",D.bk,B.dgJ)
B.c4B=new A.jW("Hot left, cold right","On a faucet, hot is on the left and cold on the right. Hot lines are marked red and cold lines blue.")
B.c4O=new A.jW("The P-trap","The curved pipe under a sink always holds a little water. That water seal stops sewer gas coming up the drain.")
B.c4Z=new A.jW("Shut-off valves","Every sink and toilet has its own small valve, so you can stop the water to one fixture without turning off the whole house.")
B.c4H=new A.jW("Slip nuts","Drain joints are sealed by a washer and a slip nut. Tighten by hand and a quarter turn: too much force cracks plastic.")
B.c4G=new A.jW("Wax ring","A toilet sits on a wax ring that seals it to the floor drain. A toilet is lowered straight down once, and cannot be slid around.")
B.c4W=new A.jW("Drain slope","Drains fall about 1/4 inch per foot so water and waste keep moving. Too flat and it clogs, too steep and the water leaves the solids behind.")
B.c50=new A.jW("Order of work","Plumbing goes from the top down on the drain (tailpiece, trap, arm) and from the wall out on the supply (valve, hose, fixture).")
B.cmT=w([B.c4B,B.c4O,B.c4Z,B.c4H,B.c4G,B.c4W,B.c50],x.Z)
B.c56=new A.Nw("Plumbing basics","\ud83d\udeb0",D.cn,B.cmT)
B.c4D=new A.jW("Studs","Studs are the vertical 2x4 posts inside a wall, 16 inches apart from centre to centre. Everything is fixed to them.")
B.c4R=new A.jW("Drilling studs","Holes for cable go through the middle of the stud, so a nail or screw cannot reach the wire.")
B.c4I=new A.jW("Drywall","A sheet is 4 feet wide, so its edges land on studs 48 inches apart. Screws go into studs only, just under the paper.")
B.c4L=new A.jW("Taping and mud","Seams get paper tape and three thin coats of joint compound, sanded smooth between coats, then primer and paint.")
B.c5_=new A.jW("Order of a build","Frame, run the pipes and wires (rough-in), inspect, hang drywall, finish it, paint, then fit the fixtures and devices.")
